# SLH-M-0001 — The project name and the nomenclature

Decided by the user on 2026-11-23.

## The name

The project is **Strange Loops in HyperMarkdown**, written **SLH**. What it
invents is the inconsistent incomplete inference system, which is the
subject of the main story.

## The nomenclature

Every document that is indexed under `doc/` carries a name of the form

```
SLH-<purpose>-<id>
```

The purpose is one letter.

| Letter | Purpose | Folder | Set by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `P` | proposal | `doc/proposals/` | the user |
| `S` | story | `doc/stories/` | the user |
| `I` | issue | `doc/issues/` | the user |
| `D` | discussion | `doc/discussion/` | the user |
| `M` | memory | `doc/memories/` | proposed by the observer, approved by the user |
| `L` | ledger entry | `doc/ledger/` | proposed by the observer, approved by the user |

The id is a four-digit number, never reused. A short name follows it:
`SLH-S-0001-inconsistent-incomplete-inference-system.hmd`. A discussion and
a ledger entry carry their date between the two: `SLH-D-0001-2026-11-23`.

From the fourth discussion on, a discussion is named to the minute and ends
in its golden token, a fruit:
`SLH-D-NNNN-YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM-fruit`. The token is returned by each worker
before the discussion closes. The rule is in `doc/discussion/index.hmd`.
Decided by the user on 2026-11-23.

The id of a discussion names a folder, since a discussion is a folder with
one file for each agent. The id of every other kind names a file.

Not renamed: the concept cards, every `index.hmd`, the methodology
documents, and the notes and the roadmap under `doc/`.

## How to act on it

- Name a new document by this rule from the start.
- Refer to a document by its name, `SLH-S-0001`, and link it.
- The concept cards under `knowledge/` are not renamed. A card's name is its
  address in every link and in every claim `card#id`.
- Do not rename a document on your own: links to it have to change in the
  same step.
